  "slug": "diana-microrna-cb45",
  "summary": "Four new database releases broaden miRNA pathway, target, tissue-expression, and isoform resources with expanded species and evidence coverage.",
  "synthesis": "The four items are database resources that organise microRNA-associated evidence from complementary angles. miRPathDB 2027 extends its miRNA-pathway association atlas to rat and rhesus macaque, organises associations into three evidence tiers, and adds cross-species views with versioned downloads. miRTarBase 11.0 curates experimentally supported miRNA-target interactions and emphasises that different experimental approaches capture distinct interaction types. DIANA-miTED v2 expands a microRNA tissue expression database and integrates a healthy-tissue reference atlas. MIsoTEx is adjacent work on alternative splicing rather than a microRNA resource, classifying mammalian transcript isoforms by tissue distribution, expression stability and abundance. The common thread is the expansion of curated, cross-species and tissue-resolved reference data for comparing regulatory relationships across tissues, species and experimental modalities.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
